# The annotations of the game image $7000-$FFFF at the entry $85FD: the single source of truth for src/game/*.asm
# (kit/mkgame.py; the format is in kit/mkgame.py, class Annotations). Witness lines: "Witness: L1 N (builds)" counts the
# runs of the entry's first instruction in the recordings of case.json (kit/mkgame.py --fix-witness).
# Coordinates: the play field is 20 character rows of 32 columns; the code passes a position as BC = row (B), column (C).
@equ $5B64 EntryCopy 414 ; 414 bytes copied from EntryCopySource at the entry; the copy ends at $5D01, two bytes into BitReverse, which the entry built just before: $5D01 holds $00 instead of $80 (1 reversed)
@equ $5D00 BitReverse 256 ; each byte with its bits reversed, built at the entry: the mirrored metatiles and sprites, the cursor keys
@equ $5E00 ColumnBuffer 180 ; the column the scroll brings in at the right: 20 cells of 9 bytes, cut by the metatile drawers
@equ $5EB4 ShipShots 48 ; the ship's shots, 3 bytes each (kind, column, row): MoveShipShots
@equ $5F00 MissileA 52 ; missile record A (MoveMissileSet)
@equ $5F34 MissileB 52 ; missile record B (MoveMissileSet)
@equ $5F68 MissileC 52 ; missile record C (MoveMissileSet)
@equ $5FC1 Explosions 60 ; the explosions, 3 bytes each (frame and kind, column, row): DrawExplosions
@isub $85FE LD HL,$FFFE
@isub $BF55 LD DE,$FF2F

@module texts ; Texts and small tables in the pixel shadow's spare halves
@about The pixel shadow (the play field drawn off screen) is laid out like the screen at $6000-$77FF; the play field is 20 character rows, so in its third third only the first 128 bytes of each 256-byte pixel line are used ($7000-$707F, $7100-$717F, ... $7700-$777F) and the game keeps its texts, small tables and some code in the other halves. A text ends at the byte with bit 7 set (PrintText $C081, PrintTextNormal $C084).
$7000 b ShadowLine0 ; The pixel shadow, third third, pixel line 0 (128 bytes)
> Written and read by the sprite drawers (DrawSprite and its three variants) and copied to the screen by ScrollRows. Zeros at the entry.
$7080 t KeyPromptText ; "PRESS A KEY FOR " and the six key names DefineKeys prints
$7090 KeyNameLeft ; "LEFT"
$7094 KeyNameRight ; "RIGHT"
$7099 KeyNameUp ; "UP"
$709E KeyNameDown ; "DOWN"
$70A2 KeyNameFire ; "FIRE"
$70A6 KeyNameDetach ; "DETACH"
$70AC t PilotStandByText ; `PILOT STAND BY $`: printed after a life is lost
@res texts/pilot-stand-by.bin
$70BD t MissionOverText ; `MISSION OVER $`: printed when the last life is gone
@res texts/mission-over.bin
$70CB t ContinueText ; "C O N T I N U E" over the countdown
@res texts/continue.bin
$70DA t BeamMeterFull ; '@': a full step of the BEAM meter
$70DB t BeamMeterStep ; '>': the step being filled
$70DC b ScoreAwards 2 ; The score awards: 10 pairs (place, digit) AwardScore hands to AddScore; an eleventh, 04 05 (5000) at $70F0, no kind uses
@res tables/score-awards.bin
> Indexed by the low nibble of an enemy kind's byte 2 less 1: place 3 with the digits 1-9, then place 4 with 1 (100-900 and 1000 points; known only from the code and the score in the level recordings).
> A kind whose score nibble is 11 would read the pair 04 05 at $70F0 (5000 points), but no kind of any level has it; nibble 12 reads the zeros after it: no points (AddScore returns at E = 0).
$70F0 b ShadowLine0Tail ; 04 05 (award 11's pair, 5000 points, unused), then zeros up to the next shadow line
$7100 b ShadowLine1 ; The pixel shadow, third third, pixel line 1
$7180 t HiScoreLabel ; "HI SCORE" on the HUD
@res texts/hi-score.bin
$7188 t BeamLabel ; "BEAM-" on the HUD
@res texts/beam.bin
$718D t LifeChar ; '%': the ship icon DrawLives repeats once a life
$718E t BlankChar ; a space: DrawLives' end
$718F t LevelText ; "R TYPE LEVEL 0 ": the digit is the level LoadLevel searches for
$719C LevelDigit ; the level's ASCII digit
$719E t LoadedOkText ; "LOADED OK"
@res texts/loaded-ok.bin
$71A7 t StopTapeText ; "STOP TAPE"
@res texts/stop-tape.bin
$71B0 t StartTapeText ; "START TAPE"
@res texts/start-tape.bin
$71BA t LoadingText ; "LOADING"
@res texts/loading.bin
$71C1 b CarrierFrames ; the eight characters of a pick-up carrier's animation (k l m n o n m l), NextCarrierFrame
$71C9 t ScoreText ; the score: six ASCII digits and the space that ends the text
> AddScore adds into it digit by digit; PrintScore prints it; InsertHiScore compares it with the table.
$71D0 b ScoreDirty ; scratch flags of the score and the name entry
$71D1 FirstPlay ; 0 before the first play: StartPlay gives the fly-in once
$71D2 NameLetter ; the letter the name entry is on
$71D3 NamePos ; the place in the name being typed
$71D4 ForceShotsA ; the reflect laser's shot pairs, 3 bytes a shot (in ClearList: 12 bytes)
$71DA ForceShotsB ; the second pair
$71E0 HitCellCount ; the soft cells ($FA) gathered this frame, the index into HitCells
$71E1 HitCells ; the (column, row) of each soft cell gathered
$7200 b ShadowLine2 ; The pixel shadow, third third, pixel line 2
$7280 t RewindSide2Text ; "REWIND SIDE 2 THEN PRESS ANY KEY"
@res texts/rewind-side-2.bin
$72A0 t SearchingText ; "SEARCHING FOR " (then LevelText)
@res texts/searching.bin
$72AE t ErrorInLoadingText ; "ERROR IN LOADING"
@res texts/error-in-loading.bin
$72BE t CreditText ; "C R E D I T  5 ": the credits left
$72CB CreditDigit ; '5' at the start; a continue spends one
$72CD t PressFireText ; "PRESS FIRE BUTTON"
@res texts/press-fire.bin
$72DE t BeamMeterEmpty ; ten '<': the empty BEAM meter
@res texts/beam-meter-empty.bin
$72E8 b ContinueData ; the countdown's work bytes
$72EB ContinueRow ; the countdown's colour row, read and written by Continue
$72F0 b KeyBitTable ; the bit masks $10, 8, 4, 2, 1 ReadKey turns a half-row bit into
$72F5 b CarrierColours ; bytes CarrierDraw reads by the carrier's kind
$72FC b ShadowLine2Tail ; zeros
$7300 b ShadowLine3 ; The pixel shadow, third third, pixel line 3
$7380 b TitleStars ; the title's star states (2 bytes a star) the star task uses while the title runs
$73A8 t NoText ; "()*+ ": the font draws it as "No. " before each high-score line (PrintHiScores $76B1)
$73AD b CollapseColumns ; six bytes TitleLogo reads
$73B3 t DigitChars ; '1'-'9': the place digits of the high-score table
@module titlestate ; The star task's switches and the Kempston probe
$73BC c StarsOn ; Switch the star task on (task 0 of TaskTable)
> A = 1, then StarsSet writes it to the task's switch byte (TaskTable + 2).
> Witness: L1 47 (c1, continue, ctl-if2, ctl-kempston, ctl-sinclair, deaths-l7, gameover, hiscore, hiscore-typed, restart, l2-l8).
$73BE StarsSet ; write A to the star task's switch
$73C2 c StarsOff ; Switch the star task off
> Witness: L1 68 (boss, c1, continue, ctl-if2, ctl-kempston, ctl-sinclair, deaths-l7, ending, gameover, hiscore, hiscore-typed, restart, l1-l7).
$73C5 c PlayStars ; Point the star task at the play's star states
> Writes 0 into the star phase operand, patches the star step to LD A,2 and points the star task's state pointer at $7380.
> Witness: L1 17 (c1, ending, gameover, hiscore, l1-l7).
$73D8 c TitleStarsOn ; Point the star task at the title's star states
> Writes $3C into the star phase operand, patches the star step to LD A,8 / LD (HL),A and points the state pointer at $80D8.
> Witness: L1 47 (c1, continue, ctl-if2, ctl-kempston, ctl-sinclair, deaths-l7, gameover, hiscore, hiscore-typed, restart, l2-l8).
$73EC c ProbeKempston ; Look for a Kempston joystick: read port $1F up to 255 times
> Stores the low four bits of the first non-zero read in KempstonAbsent, or 0 when all 255 reads were 0 (a Kempston at rest). The 48K's floating bus reads non-zero, so 0 means "a Kempston is there". Called once from the entry.
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$73FE b ShadowLine4 ; The pixel shadow, third third, pixel line 4 (from $7400)
$7480 t TitleTexts ; the title page's lines: BLAST OFF AND STRIKE / THE EVIL BYDO EMPIRE / PRESS FIRE TO PLAY / 'ENTER' SELECTS KEYS / (c) 1987 BY IREM CORP.
@res texts/title.bin
$74E3 t EnterNameText ; `ENTER YOUR NAME PILOT $`
@res texts/enter-name.bin
$74FA b ControlBits ; the last control read: bit 0 left, 1 right, 2 down, 3 up, 4 fire, 5 detach (1 = pressed)
$74FB ControlMethod ; 1 Interface 2, 2 keys, 3 Kempston, 4 Sinclair / cursor, as the title's fire picked it
$74FC ControlVector ; the reader of the control method, taken from ControlVectors
$74FE b ShadowLine4Tail ; zeros
$7580 t BestPilotsText ; "TODAY'S BEST PILOTS"
@res texts/best-pilots.bin
$7593 b ForceShotTurns 9 ; four tables of 9 bytes: the next direction of a reflected laser by the cells around it (BounceShot)
$75B7 b ClearList 4 ; The blocks ClearPlayState zeroes at every start: address, length, ...; a zero word ends it
@res tables/clear-list.bin
> $4000 6144 (the screen), $7E00 640 (SolidMap), $8100 640, $8501 252 (EnemySlots), $7AD7 28 (HitList), $5EB4 332 (the shots, missiles and explosions), $8386 109 (EnemyShots and the ship's records), $71D4 12 (ForceShotsA/B), $7DF9 7 (LevelVars).
$75DD b ExplosionFrames ; the objects of each explosion kind and step, DrawExplosions
$75F5 b ShadowLine5 ; zeros, then the pixel shadow's line 5 from $7600
@module screen ; Screen helpers: the sides, the high-score table, the title colours
$7680 c ClearSides ; Paint column 0 and column 31 of the 24 attribute rows with C (0: black)
> Witness: L1 66 (boss, c1, continue, ctl-if2, ctl-kempston, ctl-sinclair, deaths-l7, gameover, hiscore, hiscore-typed, restart, l1-l8).
$7690 c ShowHiScores ; Clear the screen and show the high-score table
> ClearScreen, the black sides, the title colour task (task 4) on, then PrintHiScores.
> Witness: L1 9 (c1, gameover, hiscore, hiscore-typed).
$769B c PrintHiScores ; Print "TODAY'S BEST PILOTS" and the nine entries of HiScoreTable
> Each entry: its place digit (DigitChars), the name and the score, double height, from row 3 down.
> Witness: L1 1309 (c1, gameover, hiscore, hiscore-typed).
$76CB c CycleTitleColour ; Interrupt task 4: step the screen's colours through the INKs on a black paper
> Paints the top attribute rows with the next colour and copies them down the screen: the whole screen follows.
> Witness: L1 807 (c1, ctl-if2, ctl-kempston, ctl-sinclair, ending, gameover, hiscore, hiscore-typed, l1-l7).
$76F5 t RewindTapeText ; "REWIND TAPE"
@res texts/rewind-tape.bin
$7700 b ShadowLine6 ; The pixel shadow, third third, pixel line 6
$7780 b DefinedKeys 2 ; Six keys as (half-row port high byte, bit mask), DefineKeys / ReadKeys
@res tables/defined-keys.bin
> As loaded: $FB/1 Q, $FB/2 W, $DF/2 O, $BF/4 K, $DF/1 P, $7F/1 SPACE.
$778C w ControlVectors ; The four control readers by ControlMethod: ReadIf2, ReadKeys, ReadKempston, ReadSinclair
$7794 b DetachKey ; the joystick methods' detach key: port $7F, bit 0 (SPACE)
$7796 c TitleLoop ; The title: logo, texts and the high-score table in turn until a fire picks the control method
> Stars off, the play state cleared, TitleLogo, the title lines; DefineKeys while the title waits (ENTER defines keys); then the high-score table, polling SelectControl; round again. SelectControl leaves the loop through the stack with the method chosen.
> The two waits take C from the code before them: $0400 = 1024 turns (C = 0 from FillBlock), then $5404 = 21 508 SelectControl polls (C = 4 from ShowHiScores).
> Witness: L1 8 (c1, gameover, hiscore).
$77FF b Unused77FF ; a byte no recording reads (known only from the heatmap)
$7800 b PlayAttrs 32 ; The play field's attribute shadow: 20 rows of 32 attributes
> Written by the scroll and the sprite drawers.
@module vars ; The variables, the font and the high-score table
$7A80 b GameVars ; The variables of play
> Read and written in the play recordings; cleared in parts by ClearPlayState and ClearShipStuff.
$7A80 ColumnPtr ; the next byte of ColumnBuffer the metatile drawers write
$7A82 ScrollStep ; the step (0-7) in the 8-frame scroll cycle
$7A83 MetaColumn ; the column (0-3) of the metatile the next column is cut from
$7A84 MapColumn ; the map block column the scroll has reached: the level's position
$7A85 MapReadPtr ; the map byte the next metatile is read from
$7A87 MapBlockPtr ; the first of the 5 map bytes of the current block column
$7A89 FrameCounter ; counts the passes of the scroll (and the title colour's steps)
$7A8A IntTicks ; counts interrupts; the main loop waits until it reaches 3
$7A8B KempstonAbsent ; 0 when ProbeKempston found port $1F quiet: only then does the title take the Kempston's fire
$7A8C ExtraLives ; the extra lives given (CheckExtraLife)
$7A8D DeathTimer ; set to 32 when the ship dies; LoseLife counts it down
$7A8E ScrollHalted ; non-zero while the scroll stands (a boss, wave command 1)
$7A8F WavesHalted ; non-zero once the level's end started
$7A90 WavePtr ; the next entry of the level's wave script
$7A94 TextHeight ; 0: PrintText draws double height; 1: normal
$7A95 HitCount ; the tags gathered into HitList by the last drawing (14 at most)
$7A96 HitResult ; ProcessHits' result
$7A97 BeamMeter ; the BEAM meter's column
$7A98 ShieldTimer ; the passes the ship carries the shield ($38 at the first start, $20 at a later life, $30 from the pick-up)
$7A99 ScoreChanged ; non-zero when AddScore changed the score: CheckExtraLife prints it
$7A9A WaveOverride ; a wave command 3 value: the next wave's slot
$7A9B LevelEndTimer ; the level's end: $41 (command 5) acts at once, $3F (a boss blast) after 31 passes
$7A9C DrawTag ; the tag DrawSprite writes into SolidMap for each cell
$7A9D StarFrame ; the star task's counter
$7A9E ShooterLimit ; wave command 4: how many enemies may fire at once
$7A9F Shooters ; the enemies firing now
$7AA0 Lives ; the lives (5 at the start)
$7AA1 ShipColumn ; the ship's column (1-28)
$7AA2 ShipRow ; the ship's row (0-19)
$7AA3 ForceAttached ; the Force: 0 free, 1 at the ship's nose, 2 at its tail
$7AA4 ShipFrame ; the ship's sprite: 3 level, 2 and 4 the tilts
$7AA5 BitUpperOn ; the upper bit device is fitted
$7AA6 BitLowerOn ; the lower bit device is fitted
$7AA7 MissilesOn ; the homing missiles are fitted
$7AA8 ForceRecord ; the Force's records, 3 bytes each (state, column, row): $7AA8, $7AAB, $7AAE (ForceRecordOf)
$7AB1 BitPositions ; the bits' positions
$7ABD WeaponKind ; the Force's laser kind (the crystal's colour)
$7ABE ForceLevel ; the Force's level: 0 none, 1-3
$7ABF BeamCharge ; the beam's charge while fire is held, up to $3E (+2 a pass; $9A66 CP $40 keeps the old value at $40)
$7AC0 BeamPower ; the beam's strength left
$7AC1 Carriers ; the two pick-up carriers' records
$7AC9 BossBlast ; non-zero while the boss explodes (BossDestroyed)
$7ACA BossBlastCount ; the random explosions left
$7ACB BossBlastPos ; the sweep position after the random ones
$7ACD RandomPtr ; the ROM pointer whose bytes are the random numbers (NextRandom)
$7ACF Scratch ; scratch words of the shot and award routines
$7AD7 HitList ; the tags the last drawing gathered (15 bytes)
$7AE7 MissileLaunch ; the missiles' launch records, 6 bytes each ($7AE7, $7AED)
$7AF0 b Font 8 ; The font: 8 bytes a character from '!' (the code - $20 from $7AE8; a space draws character $3B)
@res graphics/font.bin
> PrintText draws it double height, PrintTextNormal as it is.
$7CD8 b HiScoreTable 17 ; Nine entries of 17 bytes: name (10), score (6 ASCII digits), $A0 (bit 7 ends the text)
@res texts/hiscores.bin
> InsertHiScore inserts a new score, shifting the lower entries down; the names as loaded are the defaults.
$7D71 b HiScoreSpare ; the 17 bytes past the ninth entry the insertion shifts the last entry into (no recording reads them)
@res leftovers/hiscore-spare.bin
$7D82 b MissileFrames ; The homing missile's frame lists: (sprite, step) pairs, $FF ends a list
$7D98 MissileTurns ; the lists by direction ($7D98, $7D9B, $7D9F, $7DA6, $7DAA)
$7DB1 AntiAirPathUp ; the upward anti-air shot's path: (row step, sprite) pairs, $63 ends
$7DD6 AntiAirPathDown ; the downward path
$7DF9 b LevelVars ; seven bytes the levels' own code uses; cleared at each start
$7E00 b SolidMap 32 ; The collision map: one byte a cell of the 20 x 32 play field, the tag of what is there
> 0 empty; small values the ship and its shots; $80 + slot an enemy; $FA an enemy's soft part; $FB-$FF hard scenery (from the metatile attribute's bit 7). GetCell reads it.
$7EE2 EntryCopySource ; the 414 bytes the entry copies to EntryCopy before SolidMap is first cleared
$8080 b RowTable 4 ; The 20 play rows: (screen address, attribute address) of each row's right end
> ScrollRows walks it; the star task starts at its second row.
$80D0 b RowTableEnd ; zeros after the table
$80D8 b PlayStarStates ; the play's star states (2 bytes a star) for the star task
$8100 b DrawnMap ; 1 where a sprite cell is on the screen (set by ScrollRows' copy, cleared by its erase); the star task draws only where it is 0 (640 bytes cleared by ClearPlayState)
@module intro ; The loading screen scroller
$814F c ShowLoadingScreen ; Show the title picture and scroll the credits along the bottom
> Copies TitleScreen (6912 bytes) to the screen; then each character of ScrollerText in turn is printed at the right of the bottom rows and the rows scrolled left (ScrollRowLeft) with a HALT a step, until the text's last character; then a wait.
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$8198 c ScrollRowLeft ; Scroll 32 bytes of pixel lines left by one pixel (RL (HL) from the right end)
> Witness: L1 7440 (c1).
$81A9 t ScrollerText ; `STOP THE TAPE $` and the credits: R TYPE, PROGRAMMED BY BOB PAPE, GRAPHICS, SOUND, IREM 1987, ELECTRIC DREAMS 1988
@res texts/scroller.bin
$837B b ScrollerEnd ; eight zeros after the text
$8383 c Im2Jump ; The IM 2 target: JP Interrupt (every vector of Im2Table is $83, so the CPU jumps to $8383)
> Witness: L1 159333 (boss, c1, continue, ctl-if2, ctl-kempston, ctl-sinclair, deaths-l7, ending, force, gameover, hiscore, hiscore-typed, pause, restart, l1-l8).
$8386 b EnemyShots 3 ; The enemy shots, 3 bytes each (direction and kind, column, row): MoveEnemyShots
$83DA ShipTrail ; the ship's last positions for the bits (TrailPoint)
$83E2 BeamShot ; the beam shot: length, row, column
$83E5 AntiAirShots ; the two anti-air shot records ($83E5, $83E9)
$83ED MissileTimer ; frames before the missiles may fire again
$83F2 ShipEntry ; the ship's fly-in: 1 flying in, 2 turning back, 0 done
$83F3 BeamHudText ; the HUD text DrawHud prints after BEAM-
$8400 Im2Table ; the IM 2 vector table: 257 bytes of $83
$8501 EnemySlots ; 28 enemy slots of 9 bytes: flags, position, script and kind pointers, movers
@module main ; The entry, the main loop and the start of a life
$85FD c Entry ; The game's entry from the loader's tail: build the tables, show the title picture, load level 1, run the title
> Interrupts off; SP = $FFFE; builds BitReverse; copies EntryCopySource to EntryCopy; IM 2 through Im2Table; ProbeKempston; ShowLoadingScreen; LoadLevel loads level 1. Then NewGame, StartLife, MainLoop.
> Witness: L1 1 (c1).
$8634 NewGame ; a new game: the restart point, the score and lives reset, the title loop
$863D StartLife ; a life starts: stars on, the play state cleared, the level drawn from its restart column, the ship placed
$8649 MainLoop ; one pass of the game (the calls in order below), then wait for the third interrupt
$8656 MainLoopPatch ; three NOPs
$868C MainWait ; wait until IntTicks reaches 3
$8696 c RestartPoint ; Copy the level's first restart column and wave entry into the live ones
> Witness: L1 11 (c1, deaths-l7, gameover, hiscore, l2-l8).
$86A9 c NewGameState ; Lives = 5, ExtraLives = 0, the sound silenced, the score set to "000000"
> Witness: L1 4 (c1, continue, gameover, hiscore).
$86C3 c ClearPlayState ; Zero the ClearList blocks, set the colours and the control reader
> Zeroes every ClearList block; attributes and PlayAttrs $47; border black; clears ShieldTimer, the title colour task, the controls patch at ShieldControls, Shooters, MissileTimer and the death patch at ShipDies + 3; ControlVector from ControlVectors by ControlMethod; ResumeWaves.
> Witness: L1 64 (c1, continue, ctl-if2, ctl-kempston, ctl-sinclair, deaths-l7, ending, gameover, hiscore, hiscore-typed, restart, l1-l8).
$8721 c StartPlayField ; Start the play field at the level's restart column
> Clears ScrollHalted and the BEAM meter, takes MapColumn and WavePtr from the restart point, DrawFirstScreen, stars on, DrawHud, the black sides.
> Witness: L1 47 (c1, continue, ctl-if2, ctl-kempston, ctl-sinclair, deaths-l7, gameover, hiscore, hiscore-typed, restart, l2-l8).
@module scroll ; The scroll: map, metatiles, the shadow and the column buffer
