@module levelspace ; The level space: what the loader left where each level is loaded
@about LoadLevel loads each level's body to $C4AE; at the entry the space holds what the loader left: zeros, a stale copy of loader bytes and the title picture ShowLoadingScreen shows. Each level's own source is src/levelN.
$C4AE b LevelSpace ; The level header and body (zeros at the entry)
$C4AE LevelRestartColumn ; the block column a life restarts at
$C4AF LevelRestartWave ; the wave script entry a life restarts at
$C4B1 LevelChecks ; three checkpoint columns
$C4B4 LevelWaves ; the wave script's start and the checkpoints' entries
$C4BA LevelObjects ; the level's object table (LevelObject)
$C4BC LevelMetatiles ; the map, the metatiles below it (MetatileAddress)
$C4BE LevelKinds ; the enemy kinds (StartWave)
$C4C0 LevelMoves ; the first movers (MoveEnemies)
$C4C2 LevelMoves2 ; the second movers
$C544 b LoaderLeftover ; bytes the loader's last moves left, never read before a level overwrites them
@res leftovers/loader-leftover.bin
$DD18 b TitleScreen ; The title picture (a `SCREEN$`) ShowLoadingScreen copies to the screen
@res screens/title.scr
$F818 b LevelSpaceTail ; the bytes after the picture up to the sound's stack: level 1 loads over $F818-$F859; no play recording reads the rest
@res leftovers/level-space-tail.bin
$F872 b SoundStack ; ten bytes the tone commands use as a stack (LD SP,$F87A: the four voice periods pushed, TonePlayer reads them from $F872); read in every play recording
