$FB66 b SoundData ; The sound data: note periods, the channel slots, the command table ($FBEB), the script table ($FC0B)
> The script table at $FC0B holds 35 words, sounds $00-$22. By the code that starts them (the run counts of the starting instruction over all recordings): $00 silence (Silence, CommandWave); $01 shot (ShotSound, 3940 runs); $02 beam charging (FireBeam, 90); $03 a level 8 wave sound (wave command 6 at columns 35, 41, 48); $04 enemy hit (EnemyHit, 2492); $05 beam released (BeamRelease, 143); $06 missiles (FireMissiles, 482); $08 small explosion, $0A middle explosion, $09 big explosion (AwardScore by the enemy's size with bits $82, the first free channel, TimbreHigh: size $10 to $08, $40 to $0A, $20 and $30 to $09;, 1377/848/747; BossDestroyed's $09 or $0A never ran); $09 also the ship hit (ShipDies, 38); $0A also a life lost (LoseLife, 37) and the level 7 wave sound (columns 73-74, 94); $0B a key defined (DefineKeys, DefineKey: never ran); $0C the best pilots table entered (InsertHiScore, 10); $0D pick-up (TakePickup, 20); $0E extra life (ExtraLifeSound, 6); $0F a soft cell hit (ProcessHitsNext, 717); $10-$13 the level 2 wave sounds (columns 31-90: the boss's beat); $14 the Force docks (ForceDraw 1; ShieldControls never ran); $15 the level's end tune (LevelEnd, 8); $16 the name entered (InsertHiScore, 1); $18 a shot bounced off the scenery (BounceShot, 1576: one Chord1 step at about 1900 Hz, bits $41; it shares its script $5BD0 with the unused $17); $19, $1D, $1E the control method chosen (SelectControl, 3 each); $1A, $1B mission over (MissionOver, 4 each); $1C the Force on the ground (ForceGround, 507); $22 the CONTINUE count (Continue, 21).
> Sounds $07, $17 (the same script as $18) and $1F-$21 are started by no code and no wave script: known only from the table. $15-$1E have their scripts at $5B64-$5CFF, $1F-$21 at $F168-$F35C inside the level space (whatever the loaded level holds there), $22 at $72E8.
> The command table at $FBEB: 16 words: 0 End, 1 Rest (SoundNop), 2 Mark, 3 Back, 4 Repeat, 5 Loop, 6 spare bytes $F9C7, 7 Noise, 8-13 Chord1-6, 14-15 spare chord variants $FB0F/$FB1F (no script uses them).
@res sound/sound-data.bin
